{"id":"7db205a092ab400097ad8192207e92c2","model":"gpt-oss-120b","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"answer\": \"International Association of Athletics Federations (IAAF)\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    [\"Women's 100 metres world record progression\", 1],\n    [\"Women's 100 metres world record progression\", 2]\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to answer: \"What is the company that currently recognizes the sprinting records set by Leni Junker and Florence Griffith-Joyner?\" The question asks for the \"company\" that currently recognizes the sprinting records set by Leni Junker and Florence Griffith-Joyner.\n\nWe have evidence about world record progression: \"The first world record in the 100 metres sprint for women was recognised by the Fédération Sportive Féminine Internationale (FSFI) in 1922.\" Then \"The FSFI was absorbed by the International Association of Athletics Federations (IAAF) in 1936.\" Then \"The current record is 10.49 seconds set by Florence Griffith-Joyner in 1988.\"\n\nThus the current record (Florence Griffith-Joyner) is recognized by IAAF (now World Athletics). The question: \"company that currently recognizes the sprinting records set by Leni Junker and Florence Griffith-Joyner?\" Leni Junker set a world record in 110 yards in 1925. That record would have been recognized originally by FSFI, then after absorption by IAAF, IAAF would be the current recognizing body. So answer: International Association of Athletics Federations (IAAF). The evidence: sentence 1 about FSFI absorbed by IAAF, and sentence 2 about current record set by Florence Griffith-Joyner. Also Leni Junker set a world record earlier; but we don't have explicit mention that IAAF recognizes it now, but logically after absorption, IAAF is the governing body. Use evidence: FSFI absorbed by IAAF (sentence 1) and current record is set by Florence Griffith-Joyner (sentence 2). So answer: International Association of Athletics Federations (IAAF). Provide citations: from \"Women's 100 metres world record progression\" sentences 1 and 2.\n\nThus JSON: {\"answer\":\"International Association of Athletics Federations (IAAF)\",\"citations\":[[\"Women's 100 metres world record progression\",1],[\"Women's 100 metres world record progression\",2]]}"},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1425,"completion_tokens":482,"total_tokens":1907,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791972424,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}